**Amendment (Foundation public witnesses and integration layout)** · `amend:testing:foundation-layout` Refines (`dec:harness:levels`) for the existing foundation packages: tests/public.rs remains the external public-surface binary and tests/integration.rs remains the composition entry point. Focused sibling integration binaries are also declared integration suites in the checked registry: interchange keeps companion, deterministic_encoding, documents, inclusion, labels, prefix, properties, registry, restraint, satisfaction, theories, vectors, versions and benchmark_correctness; documents keeps panic_contract. Their tests/support modules and corpus files are support inputs, not executable suites. CLI common, execwrap and testkit use only the two standard external binaries. One focused public-surface witness suffices for each present package to distinguish external usability from internal access: interchange checks consumed prefix extent versus strict decoding; CLI common checks escaped control-record round-trip; execwrap checks empty-command refusal before effects; documents checks the public report schema; testkit checks complete named adapter results after failure. These witnesses do not claim exhaustive API coverage: the separately declared external composition suites supply the broader behavior and failure-boundary checks, and new public contracts must add their own evidence. No internal-module test is promoted to public-surface merely by its name.

